// Builtins in the agents namespace. Today: one builtin (`agent`)
// that asynchronously invokes a DSL-registered agent. See
// dsl/_reference/_agent.memql for the agent primitive itself and
// docs/planning/agents-dsl-primitive.md for the phased implementation
// plan.

// ---- builtin agent --------------------------------------------------
//
// Invoke a DSL-registered agent by name to do work. ALWAYS
// asynchronous: the call creates a v1:planner:plan with
// kind="agentInvocation", queues it, and returns the plan id
// immediately. The planner's agent loop picks the Plan up async and
// drives the agent's tool loop.
//
// Callable from any DSL context that supports builtin calls --
// automations, logic functions, policies. NEVER blocks.
//
// For blocking AI work from DSL, use `ai("promptName", args)` --
// that's the synchronous structured-output path. `agent()` is for
// agent-orchestrated, tool-using, planner-tracked work; `ai()` is
// for one-shot LLM calls with no tools.
//
// Args:
//   name     The agent's registry name (e.g. "assistant" --
//            typically the roleSlug). Must match an entry in the
//            AgentRegistry; the handler returns an error listing
//            registered names when no match is found.
//   prompt   Free-form prompt describing what you want the agent
//            to do. The agent's tool loop reads this as the user's
//            instruction; references to entities (attachmentId,
//            partitionId, etc.) are resolved by the agent's tools via
//            queries.
//   partitionId  Required by the planner -- the space the Plan lives in.
//            Callers without a space context can pass the system
//            placeholder (a future iteration may relax this).
//
// Returns one MemoryNode whose payload is
//   { planId: string, agent: {name, role, roleSlug} }
// The caller can subscribe to graph.node.updated.v1:planner:plan
// filtered by id==<planId>, or query the Plan later via
// planById, to observe progress + read Plan.output on success.

/// Async-invoke a DSL-registered agent by name. Creates a queued v1:planner:plan
/// (kind=agentInvocation) and returns its id. Use ai() for blocking LLM calls; agent() is for
/// agent-orchestrated work that runs through the planner.
@executor("integration.agents.invoke")
@args(profile="object")
builtin agent {
  name     string!
  prompt   string!
  partitionId  string!
}

// ---- builtin askSpecialist ------------------------------------------
//
// Synchronous specialist query. The assistant calls this via the
// askSpecialist tool when it wants a specialist's structured answer
// to a question. Resolves the specialist by roleSlug, invokes the
// askSpecialist structured-output prompt, returns the JSON response.
//
// Specialists never speak to humans directly; their reply lives in
// the tool result. The assistant paraphrases response.response into
// the human-facing reply.

/// Synchronously query a specialist agent by role. Returns ONE JSON object {response, rationale?,
/// confidence, needsMore?}. Specialists never write utterances; the assistant translates response
/// to a human reply.
@executor("integration.agents.askSpecialist")
@args(profile="object")
builtin askSpecialist {
  role     string!
  query    string!
  context  object
}

// ---- builtin ensureAgentForGoal --------------------------------------
//
// Factory builtin invoked by the Assistant's `ensureAgent`
// tool (dsl/agents/tools/ensureAgent.memql). Resolves a free-form
// goal into an agent ready to handle it:
//
//   - Analyzes the goal via the agentFactoryAnalyze structured-output
//     prompt against the role catalog + the user's existing agents.
//   - action="match": returns the existing agent id verbatim.
//   - action="extend": unions missing locked/relevant domains + tools
//     onto an existing same-role agent via updateAgent, then
//     returns its id.
//   - action="create": composes capabilities from the chosen role's
//     locked + default + analysis-supplied sets and writes a new
//     v1:agents:agent row via createAgent.
//
// Returns one MemoryNode whose payload is
//   { agentId, agentName, roleSlug, action, reasoning }.
// Synchronous from the caller's perspective -- the factory completes
// the write before returning so the GA can immediately invoke the
// resulting agent via `agent("name", "prompt", partitionId)`.

// ---- builtin requestUserFeedback -------------------------------------
//
// Bridges the requestUserFeedback tool (dsl/agents/tools/
// requestUserFeedback.memql) to the agents Go integration's
// `requestUserFeedback` capability. The integration transitions the
// active Plan (planId is auto-stamped by the agent streaming loop's
// agentContextStamps, so the LLM never has to supply it) to
// status=awaitingFeedback / feedbackReason=feedback_required via
// requestPlanFeedback, and returns a small ack payload
// {status:"awaiting_user", planId, kind}.
//
// Mirrors the worker integration's requestComputerUseScope /
// agentworkerRequestScope pair (the scope_elevation_required
// variant); this is the generic feedback_required variant.

/// Transition the active Plan to awaitingFeedback (feedbackReason=feedback_required) with a
/// feedbackRequest{question, kind, options?, timeoutAt}. The agent calls this when it needs the
/// user to supply missing detail mid-task; the user's answer (stamped via Plan.feedbackResponse +
/// status->running) resumes the Plan through the existing planner re-invocation path.
@executor("integration.agents.requestUserFeedback")
@args(profile="object")
builtin requestUserFeedback {
  question     string!
  kind         string!
  options      []object
  timeoutAt    string
  agentId      string!
  ownerUserId  string!
  planId       string!
  partitionId      string
}

/// Match-extend-or-create an agent that can handle the given goal. Reads the role + domain + tool
/// catalogs, runs agentFactoryAnalyze, issues the appropriate write, and returns {agentId, action,
/// reasoning}. Planner-driven callers (integrations/planner/agent_loop.go) pass `planId` so the
/// factory can stamp `lineage.originatingPlanId` on the created specialist (memql#399); the
/// GA-driven `ensureAgent` tool omits it -- the resulting specialist still lands with
/// `kind="specialist"` (the factory only ever creates specialists, never assistants or system
/// agents) but without a Plan back-pointer.
@executor("integration.agents.ensureForGoal")
@args(profile="object")
builtin ensureAgentForGoal {
  goal         string!
  ownerUserId  string!
  partitionId      string
  planId       string
}

// ---- builtin produceArtifact -----------------------------------------
//
// Backs the Assistant's `produceArtifact` tool (dsl/agents/tools/
// produceArtifact.memql). Mints a v1:planner:plan (kind="produceArtifact",
// triggerSource="user.implicit") via createPlan and returns a small
// ack {status:"delegated", planId, ack}. The plan auto-runs (the planner
// agent loop auto-starts produceArtifact plans, skipping the manual Run gate),
// so the deliverable is produced + landed in the Library asynchronously while
// the Assistant just acks and ends its turn. Mirrors the requestUserFeedback
// builtin's "mutate a Plan from the agents integration, return an ack" shape.

/// Delegate a produce-an-artifact request to the planner. Mints a v1:planner:plan
/// (kind=produceArtifact, triggerSource=user.implicit) carrying the goal + desired format/filename
/// in Plan.input, and returns {status:"delegated", planId, ack}. The plan auto-runs; the
/// deliverable lands in the Library asynchronously.
@executor("integration.agents.produceArtifact")
@args(profile="object")
builtin produceArtifact {
  goal         string!
  format       string
  filename     string
  agentId      string
  ownerUserId  string!
  partitionId      string!
}
